[{:db/id 17592186229139 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-778954fe-ed65-5c0c-8ec0-4af91a3c5254"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-778954fe-ed65-5c0c-8ec0-4af91a3c5254" :question/id #uuid "778954fe-ed65-5c0c-8ec0-4af91a3c5254" :question/math-academy-id "q-65034" :question/problem "Suppose that $L$ is a linear differential operator such that $L({y}_{1})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ and $L({y}_{2})=6{sin}^{2}⁡x$ for some functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ What is $L(3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})?$\n\n*Hint: Use $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x.$*" :question/worked-solution "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}(x)+b{y}_{2}(x))=aL({y}_{1}(x))+bL({y}_{2}(x))\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) & =3L({y}_{1})+L({y}_{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+6{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)+6{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3{cos}^{2}⁡x-3{sin}^{2}⁡x+6{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-791b9ce7-4692-5ad8-92b4-b167c4d8c95a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-791b9ce7-4692-5ad8-92b4-b167c4d8c95a" :answer-field/id #uuid "791b9ce7-4692-5ad8-92b4-b167c4d8c95a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f1d07edd-e0ca-5ec2-aa7a-e9a22bae9bf2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1d07edd-e0ca-5ec2-aa7a-e9a22bae9bf2" "answer-832a71bb-740c-5837-bd06-f7b2def0d007" "answer-ac8d1e44-2324-5ca1-81cd-0fb6177f326d" "answer-6b0ac887-1d41-58d2-bbd4-7ddbeab3e275" "answer-1affdab9-1b52-5da7-9d2f-106390720503"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1d07edd-e0ca-5ec2-aa7a-e9a22bae9bf2" :answer/id #uuid "f1d07edd-e0ca-5ec2-aa7a-e9a22bae9bf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-832a71bb-740c-5837-bd06-f7b2def0d007" :answer/id #uuid "832a71bb-740c-5837-bd06-f7b2def0d007" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac8d1e44-2324-5ca1-81cd-0fb6177f326d" :answer/id #uuid "ac8d1e44-2324-5ca1-81cd-0fb6177f326d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b0ac887-1d41-58d2-bbd4-7ddbeab3e275" :answer/id #uuid "6b0ac887-1d41-58d2-bbd4-7ddbeab3e275" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1affdab9-1b52-5da7-9d2f-106390720503" :answer/id #uuid "1affdab9-1b52-5da7-9d2f-106390720503" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8d7d4653-1949-5012-bba8-de86196b5589" "question-d74a3e3c-e2b0-50fc-9e27-1744209e35b1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8d7d4653-1949-5012-bba8-de86196b5589" :question/id #uuid "8d7d4653-1949-5012-bba8-de86196b5589" :question/math-academy-id "q-337766" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nI. ${D}_{1}(y)={y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy$\n\nII. ${D}_{2}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y$\n\nIII. ${D}_{3}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the first term is ${y}^{2},$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=x,{f}_{1}(x)=-2x,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=3.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the second term is $y,$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f3856639-8cc5-5769-ab2a-9f53121ca700"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f3856639-8cc5-5769-ab2a-9f53121ca700" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3856639-8cc5-5769-ab2a-9f53121ca700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d7ac5fcd-d0e0-5666-8e83-23100e4bb34a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1df3fa27-db87-5d4f-a0be-23a81125c98c" "answer-16f1d4a5-53db-5cf6-bc1b-078445acab5c" "answer-d7ac5fcd-d0e0-5666-8e83-23100e4bb34a" "answer-567e86ad-0a32-55a9-8b19-931ce53e8d20" "answer-fedca91d-70a4-5b6b-a4d0-9dd643119950"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1df3fa27-db87-5d4f-a0be-23a81125c98c" :answer/id #uuid "1df3fa27-db87-5d4f-a0be-23a81125c98c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16f1d4a5-53db-5cf6-bc1b-078445acab5c" :answer/id #uuid "16f1d4a5-53db-5cf6-bc1b-078445acab5c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7ac5fcd-d0e0-5666-8e83-23100e4bb34a" :answer/id #uuid "d7ac5fcd-d0e0-5666-8e83-23100e4bb34a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-567e86ad-0a32-55a9-8b19-931ce53e8d20" :answer/id #uuid "567e86ad-0a32-55a9-8b19-931ce53e8d20" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fedca91d-70a4-5b6b-a4d0-9dd643119950" :answer/id #uuid "fedca91d-70a4-5b6b-a4d0-9dd643119950" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d74a3e3c-e2b0-50fc-9e27-1744209e35b1" :question/id #uuid "d74a3e3c-e2b0-50fc-9e27-1744209e35b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-337767" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nI. ${D}_{1}(y)=3\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{x}^{2}y$\n\nII. ${D}_{2}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n\nIII. ${D}_{3}(y)={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y$" :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)=3$ and ${f}_{0}(x)={x}^{2}.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the second term is $y,$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a third-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}(x)={x}^{2},{f}_{2}(x)=0,{f}_{1}(x)=-1,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1ea9415e-b935-5b01-a9af-fa81c603a9ef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1ea9415e-b935-5b01-a9af-fa81c603a9ef" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ea9415e-b935-5b01-a9af-fa81c603a9ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d944eb4d-0a4c-5e50-915a-2fdd108bb5a2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d944eb4d-0a4c-5e50-915a-2fdd108bb5a2" "answer-58989a8c-0f59-5641-920d-959052362e5e" "answer-a7e61d62-cdc4-5531-aa2f-3ea820faba0a" "answer-884f87d0-cc4b-5052-8f16-9f1691264cfa" "answer-f97048dc-d665-5674-a86a-01f4a85a0cdc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d944eb4d-0a4c-5e50-915a-2fdd108bb5a2" :answer/id #uuid "d944eb4d-0a4c-5e50-915a-2fdd108bb5a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58989a8c-0f59-5641-920d-959052362e5e" :answer/id #uuid "58989a8c-0f59-5641-920d-959052362e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7e61d62-cdc4-5531-aa2f-3ea820faba0a" :answer/id #uuid "a7e61d62-cdc4-5531-aa2f-3ea820faba0a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-884f87d0-cc4b-5052-8f16-9f1691264cfa" :answer/id #uuid "884f87d0-cc4b-5052-8f16-9f1691264cfa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f97048dc-d665-5674-a86a-01f4a85a0cdc" :answer/id #uuid "f97048dc-d665-5674-a86a-01f4a85a0cdc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311885 :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nI. ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{1}{x+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,y$\n\nII. ${D}_{2}(y)=\\sqrt{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y$\n\nIII. ${D}_{3}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{e}^{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,y$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-083d5c44-88fc-52b7-9ce7-a90d46faa793" :activity/id #uuid "083d5c44-88fc-52b7-9ce7-a90d46faa793" :activity/title "Linear Differential Operators" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050537 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-b82a8080-41c2-564b-9e71-63af3ded9cfe" "step-8ff49c84-4dd2-5afa-9c91-bf97260b2e13" "step-d6c2288c-a7d2-5f5f-b0a9-7520017d44ee" "step-da11109d-9a7c-5a37-af06-a3bbc698126b" "step-0bacce76-2ae6-55fc-9d26-5d89fee1a2c9"] :activity/first-step "step-b82a8080-41c2-564b-9e71-63af3ded9cfe" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-b82a8080-41c2-564b-9e71-63af3ded9cfe" :step/id #uuid "b82a8080-41c2-564b-9e71-63af3ded9cfe" :step/content "question-778954fe-ed65-5c0c-8ec0-4af91a3c5254" :step/next "step-8ff49c84-4dd2-5afa-9c91-bf97260b2e13" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8ff49c84-4dd2-5afa-9c91-bf97260b2e13" :step/id #uuid "8ff49c84-4dd2-5afa-9c91-bf97260b2e13" :step/content 17592186265817 :step/next "step-d6c2288c-a7d2-5f5f-b0a9-7520017d44ee" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d6c2288c-a7d2-5f5f-b0a9-7520017d44ee" :step/id #uuid "d6c2288c-a7d2-5f5f-b0a9-7520017d44ee" :step/content "question-8d7d4653-1949-5012-bba8-de86196b5589" :step/next "step-da11109d-9a7c-5a37-af06-a3bbc698126b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-da11109d-9a7c-5a37-af06-a3bbc698126b" :step/id #uuid "da11109d-9a7c-5a37-af06-a3bbc698126b" :step/content "question-d74a3e3c-e2b0-50fc-9e27-1744209e35b1" :step/next "step-0bacce76-2ae6-55fc-9d26-5d89fee1a2c9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0bacce76-2ae6-55fc-9d26-5d89fee1a2c9" :step/id #uuid "0bacce76-2ae6-55fc-9d26-5d89fee1a2c9" :step/content 17592186311885 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
